WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:02.360
This is an age where disruptions

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.485
are taking place at such a rapid

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:06.937
pace, where the company can go from

00:00:06.937 --> 00:00:09.145
leading to bleeding at the blink

00:00:09.145 --> 00:00:09.907
of an eye.

00:00:09.907 --> 00:00:11.915
&gt;&gt; It's really about designing to

00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:14.145
be agile, designing to anticipate

00:00:14.145 --> 00:00:15.044
the unknown.

00:00:15.044 --> 00:00:19.424
[MUSIC]

00:00:19.424 --> 00:00:21.641
&gt;&gt; Almost all solutions to problems

00:00:21.641 --> 00:00:23.463
out there have a technology

00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:24.262
base to it.

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:26.018
This program is geared towards

00:00:26.018 --> 00:00:28.178
executives leveraging technology to

00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:30.344
drive change across organizations.

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:31.655
&gt;&gt; From strategic vision

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:33.380
development, innovation,

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.450
scaling excellence, this program

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.175
will make me a better leader.

00:00:37.175 --> 00:00:39.138
&gt;&gt; This program exposes executives

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.889
to the cutting edge tools that

00:00:40.889 --> 00:00:42.439
are available out there.

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.397
For example, design thinking, or

00:00:44.397 --> 00:00:45.442
behavior design,

00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:47.074
to cutting edge frameworks,

00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.241
concepts, best practices out there.

00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:50.371
&gt;&gt; When we brainstorm,

00:00:50.371 --> 00:00:51.373
we put up an idea and

00:00:51.373 --> 00:00:53.005
whoever can shoot down the idea

00:00:53.005 --> 00:00:54.716
first is the genius in the room.

00:00:54.716 --> 00:00:56.513
And through design thinking,

00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:58.102
really picked up some great

00:00:58.102 --> 00:01:00.113
ways to do brainstorming better.

00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:01.315
&gt;&gt; How do we get more rapid in

00:01:01.315 --> 00:01:02.519
terms of prototyping and

00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:03.723
testing things, rather

00:01:03.723 --> 00:01:05.270
than spending six months kind of

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.761
building something only to get

00:01:06.761 --> 00:01:08.501
the feedback after we launched it?

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.713
&gt;&gt; Something as simple as

00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:11.180
understanding that we make

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.286
decisions generally 95% of the time

00:01:13.286 --> 00:01:15.019
based on emotion and instinct.

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:16.722
It's very fundamental and

00:01:16.722 --> 00:01:18.869
will absolutely carry value going

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:21.015
forward in probably all aspects of

00:01:21.015 --> 00:01:21.763
your life.

00:01:21.763 --> 00:01:23.303
&gt;&gt; It's the all star content

00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:24.774
from the GSB, no doubt.

00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:26.163
And then on top of it,

00:01:26.163 --> 00:01:27.868
it's in Silicon Valley.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:28.984
In one week you really do get to

00:01:28.984 --> 00:01:30.101
kind of capture the essence of

00:01:30.101 --> 00:01:30.961
what it's like here.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:32.747
&gt;&gt; One of the great aspects of this

00:01:32.747 --> 00:01:34.533
program is that we have time for

00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:36.527
discussion so that others who have

00:01:36.527 --> 00:01:38.108
similar problems can learn

00:01:38.108 --> 00:01:39.222
from one another.

00:01:39.222 --> 00:01:41.172
&gt;&gt; It is a completely immersive

00:01:41.172 --> 00:01:42.309
week, [LAUGH] and

00:01:42.309 --> 00:01:44.103
it's joyfully intense.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.917
&gt;&gt; Changes that are going to take

00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:47.224
place in the future in

00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:49.476
organizations or in the marketplace

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.155
are going to be led by CIOs.

00:01:51.155 --> 00:01:52.829
&gt;&gt; I think all these skills will

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:53.666
allow more and

00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:55.548
more CIOs to sit at the table with

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.432
other C level executives as been

00:01:57.432 --> 00:01:58.619
really critical and

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:00.671
driving innovation in a company.

00:02:00.671 --> 00:02:05.959
[MUSIC]

